=== HINT 1: Create suspended process ===
STARTUPINFOA si = { .cb = sizeof(si) };
PROCESS_INFORMATION pi = {0};
CreateProcessA("C:\\Windows\\System32\\notepad.exe",
    NULL, NULL, NULL, FALSE, CREATE_SUSPENDED, NULL, NULL, &si, &pi);

=== HINT 2: Get thread context ===
CONTEXT ctx = {0};
ctx.ContextFlags = CONTEXT_FULL;
GetThreadContext(pi.hThread, &ctx);
printf("RIP: 0x%llX\n", ctx.Rip);  // x64

=== HINT 3: Read PEB ImageBaseAddress ===
// NtQueryInformationProcess(ProcessBasicInformation=0) gives PEB pointer
pNtQIP NtQIP = (pNtQIP)GetProcAddress(GetModuleHandleA("ntdll.dll"),
                                       "NtQueryInformationProcess");
PROCESS_BASIC_INFORMATION pbi = {0};
NtQIP(pi.hProcess, 0, &pbi, sizeof(pbi), NULL);

// PEB.ImageBaseAddress is at offset 0x10 on x64
PVOID imageBase = NULL;
ReadProcessMemory(pi.hProcess, (BYTE*)pbi.PebBaseAddress + 0x10,
                  &imageBase, sizeof(imageBase), NULL);
printf("ImageBase: %p\n", imageBase);

=== HINT 4: Cleanup ===
TerminateProcess(pi.hProcess, 0);
CloseHandle(pi.hThread);
CloseHandle(pi.hProcess);

=== KEY INSIGHT ===
Full hollowing requires NtUnmapViewOfSection (from ntdll) to remove the original
image, then VirtualAllocEx at the same base, WriteProcessMemory for each PE section,
patch the PEB ImageBaseAddress, set RCX/RIP to the new entry point, ResumeThread.
x64 calling convention: RCX holds the first argument - that's also the initial RIP
value the loader passes to the entry point.
Detection: hollowed processes have mismatched module list (PEB says base X, VAD says
something else) - EDRs watch for this discrepancy.
